# Page patterns

Build new pages from the existing pieces. Do not invent a second carousel, card, or heading.

- Routes stay thin. Compose in `view/`, sections in `components/reususables/`, copy in `lib/content`. The `reususables` folder name is intentional.
- The page column and the navbar share `max-w-council` (`83rem`, 1328px), with `px-5 md:px-10 min-[1408px]:px-0`. Do not give either a different cap.
- The projects page uses the news listing pieces: `PageIntro`, `NewsToolbar`, `FeaturedNewsCard`, `NewsCard`, and `SectionHeading`. A project story uses `ArticleLayout`, the same frame as a news article. The story body spans the full council column. Under the body, `PhotoGallery` shows four photographs side by side. Clicking a photograph opens it in a popup. Homepage project rows still use `HomeStoryCard`. List only verified commissioned works. New posts stay on the council Facebook page: `https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61578369553900`.
- Story rows use `HomeCarousel` with `bleed` and `autoSlide`, inside the same `max-w-council` column as the heading. Section is `overflow-x-clip`. Left edge matches the content column by measuring the column, never `100vw`.
- Cards share `HomeStoryCard`: equal size, title and description `line-clamp-2`. Story titles are `text-xl font-semibold`. Department titles are semibold and one step larger than the original card title. Projects show date and category pills. Announcements end with `Read more`. Arrows sit on the right. Add real news items when there are not enough cards to slide.
- Section titles use `HomeSectionHeading` with `titleClassName="font-bold"`. On small screens the title is `text-[26px]`; it steps up from `md`. A heading link uses the section `cta` (projects → `/projects`, announcements → `/news`).
- Wide intro copy spans the title column. Pass `descriptionClassName="max-w-none"` when the paragraph must match the heading width, as on departments. The wards heading spans the full heading row (`columnClassName="max-w-none flex-1"`). Its description is two lines, split after “verified projects,”. Ward cards are one column on small screens, two from `sm`, and five from `lg`.
- The team heading breaks as “Ikorodu Local” / “Government Team”, and its type is one step larger than the default section title. Its description is two lines, split after “professionals”.
- Keep unfinished Figma wording exactly, including `[community]` and names such as “Hon jimoh Idris iliasu” / “Chip Whip”. Replace a placeholder only when the user supplies the finished line.
- The homepage map section background stays cream through most of the block, then fades to light green (`#e0eba7`) at the bottom. The map itself is a real OpenStreetMap of Ikorodu North. Pins and the feature list use located facilities: the Isiu secretariat and marriage registry, 174 Battalion, the Lagos Ministry of Health centres that can be placed, public schools named in council and local reports, Isiu Market, and Lucky Fibres. Do not add Losi Oba PHC, Eruwen Health Post, or Olorunda PHC until a real coordinate exists. Do not restore parks, the drawn map, “ON THE MAP”, `[Council secretariat address]`, or the old placeholder counts. Clicking a feature filters the pins. “View Full Map” stays at the bottom of the feature card.
- The chairman message is the exception. It uses his published record: eight years as Vice Chairman, Executive Chairman from July 2025, and his stated priorities of infrastructure, healthcare, education, sanitation, security, youth and small-business opportunity, and open, accountable government. Do not restore the `[key focus area]` draft.
- Leave hidden Figma layers off the page (utility strip, “How can we help you?”). The shared footer keeps contact details, without office hours, the “YOUR COUNCIL. YOUR COMMUNITY.” eyebrow, “Our Contact Info.”, or the LOCATION label.
